{"id":"deferrals","ord":"a0","title":"Deferrals","desc":"How deferrals are processed (the human's rulings, 2026-08-21):\n\n- **Born from a PR.** The default is fold-in: a refactor or fix spotted while working a PR — of code it touched or a pre-existing hack — is done IN that PR. Diff size, noise, or review burden are NEVER reasons to defer (PRs here mostly merge without human review).\n- **Only a godly reason lands here**: a different subsystem, or a design the human must rule. The entry files FLAT under this node, carrying `from=<PR>` as a prop — where it came from.\n- **Triage**: each entry waits for the human's ruling — typically put to them as concrete options (the question tool), in simple words. The ruling is recorded on the node as a `ruled` prop; the node's mark then tells its state: `todo` = awaiting ruling or dispatch, `doing` = dispatched as its own lane (lane id on the orchestrator board), `done` = merged (the PR recorded), trashed = rejected.\n- **The goal state is an empty list.** A deferral is a debt with a name, not a parking spot; entries that sit here without a ruling get surfaced to the human, not accumulated.","created":"2026-08-21T17:25:18-04:00","changed":"2026-08-21T17:28:10-04:00"}
{"id":"chatentry-kind-union","parent":"deferrals","ord":"a0","title":"ChatEntry becomes a union discriminated on kind #deferral","done":"2026-08-21T19:43:21-04:00","desc":"- ChatEntry is a flat struct with a dozen kind-specific optional fields, while its own docstring claims 'a union of six kinds' — so consumers (running.ts, statusOf) must re-establish facts the type should carry (status means nothing on a non-call row; a server-defaulted field re-defaulted client-side).\n- Discriminating the wire type on kind touches the transcript writer, every consumer's narrowing, and the wire contract — a design the human must rule, not a fold-in (#324's author argued it; grok's review concurred: a standing shape, not a cleanup that work parked).","created":"2026-08-21T17:18:39-04:00","changed":"2026-08-21T19:43:21-04:00","custom":{"from":"#324","ruled":"the human 2026-08-21 ~17:3x (question tool) — TYPE-ONLY: the union is compile-time over the unchanged encoding (wire and stored bytes identical, no migration); and the consumers' now-redundant defensive re-checks are DELETED in the same PR"}}
{"id":"filter-ask-carries-revision","parent":"deferrals","ord":"a1","title":"A filtered page re-searches the whole vault every frame #needs-brainstorm #deferral","done":"2026-08-21T17:45:44-04:00","desc":"- Measured in #290 on a 90k-node vault: one bulk gesture costs nine whole-vault search calls, one per frame. No client-side coalescing window can honestly reduce it (built both ways, measured 9→8, deleted).\n- The fix is on the server side: either the ask carries the page's revision so an unmoved set is answered from what was already computed, or the narrowing moves to the server with the reading.\n- Wants a short design note first: which of the two, the wire shape, and what the reconnect re-ask becomes.","see":["reactivity-kolu-upstream"],"created":"2026-08-20T14:01:11-04:00","changed":"2026-08-21T17:45:44-04:00","custom":{"from":"olai #290 deferral","pr":"#325 merged a1302bbf — the narrowing rides the page's revision pulse; 9 whole-vault asks → 0, wire 31534→1873 kB on the 90k gesture; design note docs/brainstorming/filter-rides-the-page.md; the residual shownOf question filed as shownof-twice from=#325"}}
{"id":"shownof-twice","parent":"deferrals","ord":"a2","title":"shownOf runs twice per revision on a filtered page #deferral #human","done":"2026-08-21T17:52:31-04:00","desc":"- After #325, the narrowing rides the page's revision pulse — but computing it walks shownOf a second time per revision on a filtered page.\n- Both cures are costed in #325's design note §7: collapse to ONE member (~52 kB per keystroke against ~3 kB — declined by the author's own numbers) or a (revision, request)-keyed cache (new state no other reading has, in front of a walk that is now O(page)).\n- Wants the human's ruling: accept the double walk (it is now the right size), or buy one of the cures.","created":"2026-08-21T17:29:10-04:00","changed":"2026-08-21T17:52:31-04:00","custom":{"from":"#325","ruled":"the human 2026-08-21 ~17:5x (question tool) — ACCEPTED: the double walk is O(page) after #325 and cheap; both cures measured and neither free (one-member ~52 kB/keystroke; the cache is new state no other reading has). Closed without work; revisit only if a profile ever shows it."}}
{"id":"chat-refused-open-state","parent":"deferrals","ord":"a3","title":"The chat panel's state when a conversation could not be opened #deferral #human","done":"2026-08-21T19:37:59-04:00","desc":"- #331 fixed 'errored prompt reported as gone' for the prompt path; changeSession and boot in chat.ts still report ANY failure as status: gone — a refused session/new or session/load says 'not running' about a live agent.\n- The honest state after a refused load is not idle either: agent.ts's load-calls entered before the request, so a refusal leaves the module pointing at a conversation the agent rejected. Saying ready over that is worse than saying not running.\n- The fix needs a design ruling first: what IS the panel in when a conversation could not be opened — a distinct refused state with its own face? fall back to the previous conversation? something else?","created":"2026-08-21T19:03:19-04:00","changed":"2026-08-21T19:37:59-04:00","custom":{"from":"#331","ruled":"the human 2026-08-21 ~19:06 (question tool) — a DISTINCT REFUSED FACE: the panel gets an honest third state (couldn't open this conversation + the reason + retry), the agent still shown running, the module no longer pointing at the rejected conversation. Disposition: FOLD into #331's address round (same author, PR still open pre-review)."}}
{"id":"kolu-upgrade-headers","parent":"deferrals","ord":"a4","title":"Upstream: serveSurfaceApp exposes selected upgrade-request headers to the connection #deferral #kolu-upstream #human","todo":true,"desc":"- The live wire is a websocket; kolu's serveSurfaceApp owns the upgrade and hands no request headers to the per-connection services context — so connection-scoped identity (the trusted header at upgrade time) cannot be read there.\n- #330 works around it honestly: the chip and any plain-HTTP door (the /who endpoint, /capture) read headers directly; only a tab that should not have to GET /olai/who needs the upstream change.\n- Kolu-repo work — needs the human's ratification before any dispatch. Small: expose a selected-header allowlist on the connection context.","created":"2026-08-21T19:15:49-04:00","custom":{"from":"#330"}}
{"id":"bundle-reserved-prefix","parent":"deferrals","ord":"a5","title":"The bundle can collide with a vault: /index.html and /assets/ at the root are unreachable pages — move the bundle under a reserved prefix #deferral","todo":true,"desc":"- Since addresses became prefix-free (#256), the server hands the SPA shell to anything it does not serve itself, and the two things it serves at the root are `/index.html` and `/assets/…` (`@kolu/surface-app`). A served directory holding an `index.html` at its top level, or any file under an `assets/` folder, is a page this app can address and cannot reach — the bundle answers first.\n- Fix named in routes.ts and #256's body: move the bundle's own paths under a reserved prefix. A server change (likely touching kolu's surface-app build/serve contract — may be upstream work), which is why it was deferred. #256 said \"filed\"; it never was until 2026-08-21.","created":"2026-08-21T21:43:09-04:00","custom":{"from":"#256"}}
